Composing a Map - text formatting and location<br>Hi,<p>I&#39;d like to change the appearance of a graph produced with ggplot,<br>particularly the font face and positioning of legend and additional<br>information. This topic was partially discussed with Hadley here.<p>The crude code is bellow; It&#39;s inside a loop that manage to merge<br>appropriate data to the grid and map it.<p>I didn&#39;t change it or translate my comments but I&#39;m essentially I&#39;m<br>trying to compose the graph with additional information regarding the<br>data being presented, like the speces name in title, the min and max<br>abundances or the Season being represented, namely the lines with:<p>- scale_fill_manual(paste(&quot;Estação: &quot;, jj, &quot;
Abundâncias&quot;,<br>&quot;
Intervalo: &quot;, min_spi, &quot; - &quot;, max_spi, sep = &quot;&quot;), values = paleta,<br>labels = c(&quot;0&quot;, &quot;[1,3)&quot;, &quot;[3,5)&quot;, &quot;[5,10)&quot;, &quot;[10,25)&quot;, &quot;[25,50)&quot;, &quot;&gt;<br>50&quot;)) +<p>Can one change the location (above, below, etc) and font formatting<br>(differentially) of the text printed here?<p>- title = paste(nomeComum_i, nomeCient_i), #! Titulo do grafico<p>Is it possible to compose the sentence with regular and italic font<br>faces for common and Latin species name?<p>Code:<br>graph &lt;- ggplot(fillAb, aes(x = X1,y = X2)) +<br>              geom_polygon(aes(group = Id, fill = as.factor(classeN)),<br>colour = &quot;grey80&quot;) +<br>              coord_equal() +<br>              scale_fill_manual(paste(&quot;Estação: &quot;, jj,<br>&quot;
Abundâncias&quot;, &quot;
Intervalo: &quot;, min_spi, &quot; - &quot;, max_spi, sep = &quot;&quot;),<br>values = paleta, labels = c(&quot;0&quot;, &quot;[1,3)&quot;, &quot;[3,5)&quot;, &quot;[5,10)&quot;,<br>&quot;[10,25)&quot;, &quot;[25,50)&quot;, &quot;&gt; 50&quot;)) +<br>              scale_y_continuous(&quot;Coordenada Y&quot;) +<br>              scale_x_continuous(&quot;Coordenada X&quot;) +<br>              #! Opçoes de formataçao<br>                  opts(#!legend.position = &quot;none&quot;, - Para eliminar a<br>legenda, se necessario<br>                  title = paste(nomeComum_i, nomeCient_i), #! Titulo do grafico<br>                  plot.title = theme_text(size = 12, face = &quot;italic&quot;),<br>#! Formataçao do titulo do grafico<br>                  axis.text.x = theme_text(hjust = 0.5,vjust = 1.2,<br>size = 10,col = &quot;grey50&quot;), #! altera a formataçao do png (?)<br>                  axis.text.y = theme_text(hjust = 0.5, vjust = 0,<br>size = 10,col = &quot;grey50&quot;, angle = 90),<br>                  axis.title.x = theme_text(size = 10),<br>                  axis.title.y = theme_text(size = 10, angle = 90),<br>                  legend.title = theme_text(hjust = 0,size = 10, face = &quot;bold&quot;),<br>                  legend.text = theme_text(hjust = -0.2, size = 10)) +<br>                #! Adicionar pontos que podem representar localidades,<br>outras referencias<br>                geom_point(aes(x = X1,y = X2), colour = &quot;black&quot;,data =<br>data.frame(X1 = Loc$X1[Loc$Area == substr(hh, 1, 2)], X2 =<br>Loc$X2[Loc$Area == substr(hh, 1, 2)]), size = 2.5) +<br>                geom_text(aes(x = X1,y = X2,label = Loc$Local[Loc$Area<br>== substr(hh, 1, 2)]), colour = &quot;black&quot;,data = data.frame(X1 =<br>Loc$X1[Loc$Area == substr(hh, 1, 2)] + 900, X2 = Loc$X2[Loc$Area ==<br>substr(hh, 1, 2)] - 400), size = 4)<p>The result of the code above can be seen here<br><a href="http://img412.imageshack.us/img412/7674/emberizacalandramap.png" target="_blank" rel="nofollow" data-saferedirecturl="https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://img412.imageshack.us/img412/7674/emberizacalandramap.png&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792383871204000&amp;usg=AOvVaw142K_DwlFNbl41qABwU_rZ">http://img412.imageshack.us/img412/7674/emberizacalandramap.png</a><p>or<p><a href="http://ggplot2.googlegroups.com/web/Emberiza_calandra_map.png?gda=20LsjUsAAADSH7y5MFnpO4_MGPipxqBFfgkxB0-PWVoPhcHaWuTXdLSq1oDxkUyBnLKW235Bk0_2Jbh5tp0Wpp4RSm-5o5pQBkXa90K8pT5MNmkW1w_4BQ" target="_blank" rel="nofollow" data-saferedirecturl="https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://ggplot2.googlegroups.com/web/Emberiza_calandra_map.png?gda%3D20LsjUsAAADSH7y5MFnpO4_MGPipxqBFfgkxB0-PWVoPhcHaWuTXdLSq1oDxkUyBnLKW235Bk0_2Jbh5tp0Wpp4RSm-5o5pQBkXa90K8pT5MNmkW1w_4BQ&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792383871204000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0i1trB9gHgk7Dy08ePSo8B">http://ggplot2.googlegroups.com/web/Emberiza_calandra_map.png?gda=20LsjUsAAADSH7y5MFnpO4_MGPipxqBFfgkxB0-PWVoPhcHaWuTXdLSq1oDxkUyBnLKW235Bk0_2Jbh5tp0Wpp4RSm-5o5pQBkXa90K8pT5MNmkW1w_4BQ</a><br>(I don’t know any other way to redirect to the image uploaded to<br>google group)<p>Any help will be appreciated.<p>Paulo<p>PS.: I&#39;m not being able to post directly to the group from my google account.<br>-- <br>_______________<br>Paulo E. Cardoso<br></p></p></p></p></p></p></p></p></p></p></p></p></p></p>
